{
  "quest.5F2B5CF5364036BA.title": "Even the Ores Are Automated!",
  "quest.7603482FB49E6CDC.title": "Automate Your Crucible v0.1",
  "quest.2F6BB9CCE92566C7.quest_desc": [
    "The Item-O-Meter Sensor can precisely detect item counts, and its mode can be switched.",
    "",
    "This may be very useful for your auto-feeding system, though you can also build the feeding module without it.",
  ],
  "quest.107EF5262CC742B8.quest_desc": [
    "The Smelter can melt your materials into a molten form.",
    "",
    "Then you can feed these molten materials into a Mixer to make alloys! Very simple and easy to understand.",
    "",
    "However, some metals or materials don't actually have a \"liquid\" registered, which means alloys involving those materials can still only be made in a Crucible.",
  ],
  "quest.08E3E6DDCFDC18BA.title": "High-Speed Casting 2",
  "quest.7603482FB49E6CDC.quest_desc": [
    "This can be your first automation, and it's very simple.",
    "",
    "Design an automated system that detects the Crucible's temperature and shuts off the Burning Box when it's above the desired temperature.",
    "",
    "&mMaterials: one Piston, one Thermometer Sensor, some Red Alloy Cables&r",
    "Materials: one Thermometer Sensor, one Trapdoor",
  ],
  "quest.68270221023AC31D.title": "Automate Your Crucible v1.0",
  "quest.7BA9AA57C371CBC6.quest_desc": [
    "Automatically shutting off the fire alone may not be nearly enough for you.",
    "",
    "You also need to automatically extract products such as alloys from the Crucible. Design a simple system that outputs the molten contents into Molds once the Crucible reaches temperature.",
    "",
    "Crucible Crossings can lead the Crucible's molten fluid into &lmore&r Molds.",
    "",
    "A Monkey Wrench can set a Mold's automated input direction and whether it's under automated control (right-click the center and the edges of the Mold respectively).",
    "",
    "Materials: some Crucible Crossings, some Molds, some Red Alloy Cables",
  ],
  "quest.107EF5262CC742B8.quest_subtitle": "Automate Your Cruci... No, Wait, What Is This?",
  "quest.51D3E23708F04954.title": "Automating GT6",
  "quest.2F6BB9CCE92566C7.title": "Item-O-Meter Sensor",
  "quest.6C1745BB42167B23.title": "Hydrochloric Acid? Ore Washing",
  "quest.4AEA35C52F5D8871.title": "Automate Your Large Crucible",
  "quest.56B3AB17F8E0EF86.title": "Igniter",
  "quest.34B2D9DBEF81D5B7.title": "Automated Ore Processing",
  "quest.619B53EA839D4920.title": "High-Speed Casting 1",
  "quest.6E13368D5BBEC3CB.title": "Aqua Regia Ore Washing",
  "quest.107EF5262CC742B8.title": "High-Temperature Melting",
  "quest.619B53EA839D4920.quest_desc": [
    "A Basin can output 9 units of material at once.",
    "",
    "The Basin has no automation settings, so you need a Crucible Faucet to control whether molten material flows into the Basin.",
    "",
    "If there's less than 9 units of molten material, it can't output (take deliberate advantage of this!).",
    "",
    "The Crucible Faucet can be toggled between redstone control and no redstone control.",
    "",
    "Cast Metal Blocks can be cut directly into Plates with a Buzzsaw; together with Lubricant, this greatly saves your life.",
    "",
    "Cast Metal Blocks can also be rolled directly into Dense Plates with a Rolling Mill.",
  ],
  "quest.66BAA1D8181C9584.title": "Automated Gem Sifting",
  "quest.7DDFB77FE39B5991.title": "Sulfuric Acid Ore Washing",
  "quest.01585DF06166FF53.title": "Electric Temperature Control System",
  "quest.01585DF06166FF53.quest_desc": [
    "If you have a stable power source,",
    "",
    "you might as well try using an Electric Heater to precisely control the Crucible's temperature.",
    "",
    "This requires a Redstone Machine Switch, some Red Alloy Cables and a Thermometer Sensor.",
  ],
  "quest.08E3E6DDCFDC18BA.quest_desc": [
    "The Thermoelectric Cooler can also affect Molds and Basins.",
    "",
    "In that case its CU output side speeds up cooling, cooling the items inside to ambient temperature faster. Make one if you want that.",
    "",
    "Choose a Cooler of the appropriate voltage tier for your needs.",
  ],
  "quest.51D3E23708F04954.quest_desc": [
    "GT6 is a tech mod that can be automated.",
    "",
    "That said, GT6 can absolutely be played entirely by hand, but that will greatly wear down your patience and energy.",
    "",
    "Complete some automation content to free your hands.",
  ],
  "quest.7BA9AA57C371CBC6.title": "Automate Your Crucible v0.2",
  "quest.68270221023AC31D.quest_desc": [
    "If you've already completed the previous quests and opened this one,",
    "",
    "you must want to go further. Next you need to design an \"&l&bAuto-Feeding&r&r\" system, so your Crucible can accept new materials after outputting its products.",
    "",
    "If you understand the Crucible's mechanics, you surely know that throwing materials into the Crucible lowers its temperature. Using this, you can keep smelting alloy materials without shutting off the fire.",
    "",
    "There are many ways to implement an auto-feeding system, but most are controlled by a feeding signal.",
    "",
    "The main approach is that the feeding signal can trigger a one-time output of a certain amount of material, then wait for the next signal.",
    "",
    "You can use a Piston to turn a long signal into a pulse signal.",
    "",
    "You can output items with a GT6 Hopper / a vanilla Hopper. A regular GT6 Hopper's mode can be switched with a Monkey Wrench so it outputs a specific number of items at once, while a vanilla Hopper only outputs one item at a time.",
    "",
    "You can use a Thermometer Sensor's extension wire / a Weight-O-Meter Sensor to output the feeding signal.",
    "",
    "Choose your own materials - can you build it?",
  ],
  "quest.56B3AB17F8E0EF86.quest_desc": [
    "If you want automatic ignition, make an Automatic Igniter.",
    "",
    "It uses EU electric sparks, and the direction it faces can be ignited.",
  ],
  "quest.4AEA35C52F5D8871.quest_desc": [
    "The Large Crucible has the following unique traits:",
    "",
    "Enormous heat mass, the most interaction faces, the largest capacity for meltable contents, and a lower temperature limit than a small Crucible of the same material",
    "The top blocks can accept items, the middle layer can output molten material through Molds and Crucible Crossings, and the bottom can accept heat",
    "",
    "With these traits, the Large Crucible can melt large amounts of items, making it the best choice for smelting/shaping materials in bulk. If you're interested, you can also use a Large Crucible for automated alloying.",
    "",
    "Even so, you should still wisely choose the right Crucible for alloy smelting.",
  ],
}